Asked: Asked Claude to add a way for a student and mentor to contact each other from the connections page, since the system does not provide messaging. It surfaces connections and defers to email or external tools for communication. We wanted just an email button, plus the full updated code for InMemoryProfileData.java, connections.js and connections.html.

Produced: Claude first produced a much larger change for the whole ticket set: a session log, a notification client for Communication & Notifications, integration test scripts and new docs. For the email button on its own, it gave us three files. InMemoryProfileData.java adds studentEmail and mentorEmail from Shared Core to the connection view. connections.js gets a contactLine function that builds an "Email your mentor" or "Email your mentee" mailto button. connections.html gets the button CSS and a notice that Mentor Matching does not provide messaging.

Changed: We only took the email button for this change, not the larger version, so the commit stays small and reviewable. The session log and notifications can come in later commits once we confirm the design with Shared Core and Communication & Notifications. We kept Claude's rule that emails only show while a connection is ACTIVE, so a mentor can't see a student's email from a request they haven't accepted, and emails stop showing once the connection ends. The button is a mailto link styled as a button, because a link is what opens the user's email app. It shows the address next to it for people without a mail app set up. We still need to confirm with Shared Core that /users/{id} returns email and that sharing it between active participants is allowed.
